## 🛠️ Setup

### 📦 Install dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

### 🔗 Generate API client

Make sure the backend is running at `{{ backend_url }}`, then run:

```bash
npm run generate-api
```

This generates the TypeScript client in `src/api/client/` from the backend's OpenAPI spec.

### 🪝 Pre-commit hooks

Husky is configured to run lint-staged on every commit (ESLint + Prettier).
Hooks are automatically installed when you run `npm install` (via the `prepare` script).

## ▶️ Run locally

```bash
npm run dev
```

App will be available at [http://localhost:8080](http://localhost:8080).

## 🏗️ Build for production

```bash
npm run build
```

## 🐳 Docker

Build and run the production image:

```bash
docker build -t {{ project_name | lower | replace(' ', '-') }} .
docker run -p 8080:8080 \
  -e BACKEND_URL=https://your-api.example.com \
  {{ project_name | lower | replace(' ', '-') }}
```

The container uses `envsubst` to inject runtime environment variables into `env.js` at startup.

## 📁 Project structure

```
src/
├── api/
│   ├── apiClient.ts       # API client initialization
│   └── client/            # Auto-generated from OpenAPI (git-ignored)
├── components/
│   └── Header.tsx         # Shared navigation header
├── pages/
│   ├── index.tsx          # Page exports barrel
│   └── home/
│       ├── HomePage.tsx
│       └── components/
├── App.tsx                # Router setup
├── main.tsx               # App entry point
├── env.ts                 # Runtime environment variables
└── index.css              # Tailwind CSS v4 entry
public/
├── env.js                 # Local dev env values (not committed in prod)
└── env.template.js        # Template for envsubst in Docker
```

## 🔧 Available commands

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `npm run dev` | Start dev server on port 8080 |
| `npm run build` | Production build |
| `npm run lint` | Run ESLint |
| `npm run lint:fix` | ESLint with auto-fix |
| `npm run format` | Prettier format |
| `npm run generate-api` | Regenerate OpenAPI client |
